<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">minor-shield</ansi> spell

The <ansi fg="command">Minor Shield</ansi> spell conjures a shimmering barrier of force around the
target, bolstering their defenses against physical attacks. The barrier
absorbs incoming damage and appears in your armor rating on the status sheet.

The shield's strength scales with the caster's willpower and spellcasting
skill. More skilled casters also sustain the barrier for longer.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">cast minor-shield</ansi>              Shields yourself.
  <ansi fg="command">cast minor-shield [target]</ansi>     Shields a nearby ally.

<ansi fg="yellow">Base Folds:  </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">4</ansi>
<ansi fg="yellow">Target:      </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">Single ally (or self)</ansi>
<ansi fg="yellow">Defense:     </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">None — help spells always apply</ansi>
<ansi fg="yellow">Duration:    </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">10 rounds, +1 per 5 spellcasting skill levels</ansi>
<ansi fg="yellow">Armor bonus: </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">(willpower + spellcasting) / 3</ansi>
<ansi fg="yellow">Conv. Cost:  </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">4</ansi>
<ansi fg="yellow">School:      </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">Enhancement</ansi>

<ansi fg="white-bold">Notes:</ansi>
  - The barrier's armor bonus shows up under Armor in the <ansi fg="command">status</ansi> display.
  - The bonus applies to both incoming weapon attacks and physical spells.
  - Casting minor-shield again while a barrier is active will overwrite it.

<ansi fg="magenta-bold">See also:</ansi> <ansi fg="command">help cast</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help spells</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help heal</ansi>
